-- issue #1386: an UNRELATED interface, deliberately using a DIFFERENT method
-- name (`mthb`, not `mth`) than ifacea's `IA.mth`. main.mdk's `Blob` implements
-- ONLY this interface. Unlike #1276's fixture, there is NO bare-name collision
-- anywhere in this program: nothing but `IA` is ever named `mth`. That is the
-- point -- it isolates the defect to pass-placement (obligation-checking is
-- skipped outright for an alias-qualified occurrence), not to the witness/
-- collision table #1276 pins.
export interface IB a where
  mthb : a -> Int
